### Pro-Tip for Senior Engineers:

Whenever you see an `ORA-00904`, always check your SQL against the **actual** database metadata.

If you are ever unsure about a column name in the future, you can run this query to get a clean list of columns for any table in Oracle:

```sql
SELECT column_name 
FROM user_tab_columns 
WHERE table_name = 'WORKFLOW_TRANSITIONS';

```

Once you update that query in your Java code to use `WORKFLOW_STAGE`, the error will disappear and your workflow will proceed to Step 2 correctly!
